    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0237</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2211.07804_rag::chunk_007</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2302.10907_rag::chunk_002</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2209.02646_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2303.05334_rag::chunk_006</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2310.08442_rag::chunk_002</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2309.07867_rag::chunk_001</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2310.04041_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2209.04747_rag::chunk_019</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2309.06169_rag::chunk_001</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2306.01900_rag::chunk_002</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2310.00318_rag::chunk_002</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2211.03595_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2305.14849_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2211.17106_rag::chunk_007</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reverse Process. Leveraging the above definitions, we can approximate a reverse process to get a sample from q ( x 0 ) .</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">a reverse chain that removes the noise from the data to recover it to the original one.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the reverse process denoises the prior state back to the starting state using transition kernels</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">After the reverse diffusion process, the denoised latent variables are passed through the trained decoder D ( . ) to generate the images.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The reverse denoise process is trained to reverse the forward diffusion process in Eq. 2 by learning the denoise network.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">viewing the discretized forward and reverse processes as a fixed inference network and a learnable generator, respectively.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the joint probability of the reverse process is given by</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the usual reverse process with the determined schedule</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the errors of the approximate solutions from predicting every data state in the reverse process as one-step prediction errors.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The reverse process is defined by learned Gaussian transitions and gradually denoises the data</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">During the backward process, an image is recovered from a normal Gaussian noise by several iterations.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the reverse process denoises the prior state back to the starting state using transition kernels.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">compute approximate samples from the reverse process by running the approximate reverse process</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the reverse process entails denoising the data from noise to target data. This process is governed by a set of parameters</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the reverse process requires a cascade of lters with dynamic frequency response</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#longskipconnection">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#entity"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LongSkipConnection</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A structural component in U-Net architectures that connects shallow and deep layers.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0122</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0122</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2209.12152_rag::chunk_012</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the long skip connection is crucial while the down/up-sampling operators in CNN-based U-Net are not always necessary.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#patch_level_training_framework">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#entity"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Patch-level Training Framework</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A training framework applicable to diffusion models that utilizes patch coordinate and size conditioning to save training time and data costs.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0091</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0091</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2304.12526_rag::chunk_002</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The first patch-level training framework, generally applicable to diffusion models, that targets saving training time and data costs.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#sample_quality">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#entity"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Sample Quality</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A measure of the perceptual or statistical excellence of generated examples from a model.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0105</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0149</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0105</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0149</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2309.06169_rag::chunk_012</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2209.04747_rag::chunk_021</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2309.06169_rag::chunk_000</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">VE SDE provides better sample quality than VP SDE</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the new objective returns higher quality examples without an impact on diversity</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">challenge in balancing speed and image visual quality</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
