  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#classifier_guidance">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#entity"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Classifier Guidance</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A mechanism that leverages an extra classifier network to compute a gradient to constrain denoising networks to satisfy conditions.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0054</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0074</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0146</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0054</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0074</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0146</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2310.13102_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2307.01924_rag::chunk_005</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2306.04542_rag::chunk_016</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Similarly to how classifier guidance is applied, we modify the reverse diffusion process by adding the gradient of a potential.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Dhariwal and Nichol ( 2021 ) propose classifier guidance where the class conditional parameters ( x t | y ) and ( x t | y ) are perturbed by the gradients of a classifier p ( y | x t ) that predicts the target class y .</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Classifier guidance leverages an extra classifier network to compute a gradient as the modification on the d</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
